	S1, S2, S3 → On-board Slave Devices
	M2         → Another On-board Module
	S4         → Off-board Slave Device


* I2C is designed for multislave and multimaster communication

* Designed firstly for TV mother board 

* I2C :- 2 represents no.of pins 

* Master1 & Master2 cannot communicate with 2 slaves at the same time

* Arbitration mechanism :- Will avoid data corruption, as there is a chance both master will send, data at the same time



Arbitration Mechanism 
---------------------

* Works on the priority of master 

* Master which have higher priority will send data first, The one with lower priority will wait

* Inbuilt priority setting (user can't change)



List of I2C slaves
------------------

1. Real Time Clock (RTC)
2. EEPROM
3. Sensors
4. OLED Display 
5. ADC 
6. IO port expander, many more 




Features of I2C Protocol
------------------------

1. Designed by philips semiconductor and introduced to master since the mid 1990's 

2. Two wired communication protocol

	a) Serial Data  (SDA)				
	b) Serial Clock (SCL)			   _ Vcc	
